How big is it?

Let's ground this. A modern skyscraper like the Burj Khalifa has 160+ floors. The Loom is pre-war — built when corporations were competing for "tallest" like it was a dick-measuring contest. It was never finished. The top 20 floors are skeletal — open to the sky, wind howling through exposed girders.

